$comment
  Written by hand, not recorded, which the other dumps in this folder are not.
  A state machine needs a dump to project onto the FSM diagram, and none of the
  recorded ones has a machine in it: fsm.sv is the only fixture whose next state
  a case on itself decides, and nothing had ever simulated it.

  Kept by hand rather than generated because it is short enough to read, it is
  the same either way on every machine, and reproducing it needs no toolchain.
  Every value below follows from fsm.sv, so the two have to be edited together:

    always_ff : !rst_n -> S_IDLE, else state <= next_state
    always_comb: next_state = state, then
                 S_IDLE : start -> S_RUN
                 S_RUN  :          S_WAIT
                 S_WAIT : done  -> S_IDLE
                 default:          S_IDLE
    assign     : busy = (state != S_IDLE)

  So the run is: held in reset, released, started, one clock in S_RUN, waiting
  until done, then home. Posedges are at 10, 30, 50, 70, 90, 110.
$end
$timescale 1ns $end
$scope module tb $end
$scope module dut $end
$var wire 1 ! clk $end
$var wire 1 " rst_n $end
$var wire 1 # start $end
$var wire 1 $ done $end
$var wire 1 % busy $end
$var wire 2 & state $end
$var wire 2 ' next_state $end
$upscope $end
$upscope $end
$enddefinitions $end
